<!-- P1/P2 strict weak-address materialization before folding, with non-PIC,
large-model and mixed PIC forms. CLI replay checks zero/bound identities,
addends, independent fixed literals and exact call counts at O0/O2.

The common-* objects (common.c) hold two COMMON objects beside the weak
function. The slot allocated for the weak address once started where COMMON
storage starts, so `counter += value` printed as a write of the slot and the
test read both objects; slot space is now reserved ahead of COMMON storage.
`same` compares its argument with the weak address through one immediate that
reaches the compare's subtraction and flags, which reads the slot once. -->
<script>
<com>clear architecture</com>
<com>load file tests/fixtures/nullable-relocations/weak-n32.elf</com>
<com>read symbols</com>
<com>map prototype guard int guard(int value);</com>
<com>map prototype optional int optional(int value);</com>
<com>lo fu guard</com>
<com>decompile</com>
<com>print C</com>
<com>clear architecture</com>
<com>load file tests/fixtures/nullable-relocations/weak-64.elf</com>
